-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 48\u00b0F was the 25th warmest November 13 high (tied) of 126 since 1893, the warmest since 2025.","t_yest":"November 13: warmer than 78% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>48\u00b0F</strong> was the 25th warmest November 13 high (tied) of 126 since 1893, the warmest since 2025. The normal high for the date is 43\u00b0F, and the record is 66\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>27\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Missoula's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Missoula has set <strong>44 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 77 that chance alone would give, and <strong>104 record highs</strong>, more than the 77 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (52). Missoula's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 6, 2007.","t_chg":"Missoula's nights got warmer. Its days didn't.","p_chg":"Across 112 complete years: Missoula's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.25), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1895. Missoula's average high shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.04 to +0.14) that includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Missoula's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.03 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 14.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1998 (21.81 in); the driest, 1931 (7.44 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}